WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:02.767
Two thousand years ago,

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:05.344
the founding text of
Chinese medicine did not

00:00:05.344 --> 00:00:06.489
begin with a remedy.

00:00:06.489 --> 00:00:08.550
It began with a claim about
reality.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.842
Yin and yang. Not two
substances in two jars,

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:16.384
and not mysticism — a set
of operating rules,

00:00:16.384 --> 00:00:18.700
stated like someone
describing a machine.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.271
Yang turns things into
energy;

00:00:23.271 --> 00:00:24.790
yin finishes them into
shape.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.671
And sickness is simply the
right things standing in the

00:00:27.671 --> 00:00:28.300
wrong place.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.637
The blazing fire devours
the energy;

00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:34.895
the small fire feeds it.

00:00:34.895 --> 00:00:37.569
A fire that consumes its
own fuel is not stronger —

00:00:37.569 --> 00:00:38.250
only shorter.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.535
Five directions, five
organs, five feelings,

00:00:43.535 --> 00:00:45.968
each governing the next.
Anger injures the liver,

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:48.650
but grief overcomes anger
— the fire falls, like rain.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.348
Many of its answers turned
out wrong.

00:00:53.348 --> 00:00:55.229
The ambition did not: see
the faint sign,

00:00:55.229 --> 00:00:57.203
treat the root. The
Emperor's Inner Canon —

00:00:57.203 --> 00:00:58.350
The Great Correspondence.
